Fix `plugins/catalog-backend/src/database/operations/stitcher/buildEntitySearch.ts` for these problems, changing only what they need, following the conventions in the shared brief:
1. SECURITY — MEDIUM. The write-side `User` exclusion inspects the WRONG kind, so the two User gates are not independent and the privacy guarantee is not structural as required.

Around line 229 the code reads:

    if (entity.kind.toLowerCase() !== 'user') {
      const formerRefs = parseFormerEntityRefs(entity.metadata.annotations?.[ANNOTATION_FORMER_ENTITY_REFS]);
      for (const ref of formerRefs) {
        raw.push({ key: `${ANNOTATION_FORMER_ENTITY_REFS_SEARCH_KEY_PREFIX}${ref}`, value: true });
      }
    }

This gates on the CLAIMANT's kind. A `Component` (or any non-User kind) that declares `user:default/old-name` as a former ref therefore DOES get a synthetic row written, and that row is queryable through the ordinary entity-filter API. That is a confirm-a-guessed-former-user-name oracle: an attacker who guesses a person's previous username can confirm it by filtering on the synthetic key. The read-side refusal in resolveFormerEntityRef still blocks the redirect, so this is disclosure-by-oracle rather than privilege escalation — but the requirement is that BOTH directions are covered structurally so no later caller can re-enable it.

Fix: ALSO skip any CLAIMED REF whose kind lowercases to 'user'. Keep the existing claimant-side skip as well — both directions must be covered. So: keep the outer claimant check, and inside the loop skip each `ref` whose parsed kind is `user`. The refs produced by `parseFormerEntityRefs` are already normalized full `kind:namespace/name` strings (lowercased by stringifyEntityRef), so the claimed kind is the part before the first ':' — check it in a way that cannot be defeated by case variation, and do not introduce a throw on this path (stitching must not fail on a hostile annotation; the parse helper is already fail-closed per entry).

Change nothing else in this file: the raw-annotation row (the whole delimited string) must still be emitted as before, the MAX_KEY_LENGTH drop behaviour in mapToRows is unchanged, and the Apache 2.0 header must keep its existing year (this is an existing file — do NOT change the year).

Also address a LOW finding in the same pass if it costs nothing: a former ref whose synthetic key exceeds MAX_KEY_LENGTH (200) is silently dropped with no signal. If this file has a logger or an existing warning mechanism in scope, emit a brief warning naming the dropped ref; if there is NO logger in scope, do NOT add a dependency or change the function signature to get one — leave the behaviour as is and say so. Fail-closed semantics must not change either way.

The file's current text is under Inputs, marked "current text"; your edits apply to exactly that text.

## Answer
